e request header. Consumers will store this key in a local `ProcessedRequests` table (with 24-hour expiration) to ensure that retried messages from Kafka do not trigger duplicate database writes.\n\n### Conclusion\nThis architecture transformation effectively addresses the initial weaknesses by decoupling real-time data ingestion from transactional flows and formalizing safety-critical patterns like Sagas and CDC. This design maximizes throughput by isolating heavy telemetry loads while ensuring data integrity through strict idempotency and schema-registry-backed communication.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "extra_content": {"google": {"thought_signature": "EjQKMgG+Pvb70Uw6cXF6N3Jn0lHENr8rl2eDhbroVLZcO3WbnwBoWVX5aYmdKaR828HdrAYp"}}}}], "created": 1774274264, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1021, "prompt_tokens": 6397, "total_tokens": 7418, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": null}}, "prompt_tokens": 6397, "completion_tokens": 1021, "agent_id": null}
